abstract: >-
  Research software, three English reports (the latest is a working manuscript) and computational/formal evidence
  for a deterministic two-player shared-pool Mahjong achievement game. Complete
  SAFE-state retrograde analysis and reverse replay classify the empty position
  as a second-player win. The October 2026 V17 run evaluates all six finite
  acceptance families on all 778,532,864,302 stored labels under a kernel-proved
  original-game implication. Native execution and external bookkeeping remain
  trusted; no closed actual-input opening Lean declaration or independent
  execution replication is claimed. A separate AI source/record review is supplied. Later fixed numerical/game
  proof pilots and same-host local-delivery tests are reported, with further
  manuscript review pending and no new release created.
  Version and date above identify the immutable software release, not subsequent
  evidence-asset records; cite the exact commit for current research material.
